{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":10000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_Iran"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_Iran:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| |  |  |  |  | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | ←   * [2022](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_in_Iran \"2022 in Iran\") * [2021](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_Iran \"2021 in Iran\") * [2020](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_in_Iran \"2020 in Iran\") |  | [2023](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AD_2023 \"AD 2023\")  in  [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") | →   * [2024](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_in_Iran \"2024 in Iran\") * [2025](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_in_Iran \"2025 in Iran\") * [2026](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_in_Iran \"2026 in Iran\") | | |\n| Decades: | * [2000s](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:2000s_in_Iran \"Category:2000s in Iran\") * [2010s](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:2010s_in_Iran \"Category:2010s in Iran\") * **[2020s](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:2020s_in_Iran \"Category:2020s in Iran\")** |\n| See also: | [Other events of 2023](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023 \"2023\") [Years in Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_years_in_Iran \"List of years in Iran\") |\n\nEvents in the year **[2023](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023 \"2023\") in [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\").**\n\n* [Supreme Leader of Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Leader_of_Iran \"Supreme Leader of Iran\"): [Ali Khamenei](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\")\n* [President of Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Iran \"President of Iran\"): [Ebrahim Raisi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ebrahim_Raisi \"Ebrahim Raisi\")\n* [Speaker of the Parliament](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliament_of_Iran \"Parliament of Iran\"): [Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammad_Bagher_Ghalibaf \"Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf\")\n* [Chief Justice](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_Justice_of_Iran \"Chief Justice of Iran\"): [Gholam-Hossein Mohseni-Eje'i](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gholam-Hossein_Mohseni-Eje'i \"Gholam-Hossein Mohseni-Eje'i\")\n\n* 18 January – At least 150 people are injured by a magnitude 5.8 [earthquake](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_earthquakes_in_Iran \"List of earthquakes in Iran\") in [Khoy](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoy \"Khoy\"), [Khoy County](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoy_County \"Khoy County\"), [West Azerbaijan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Azerbaijan \"West Azerbaijan\").[[1]](#cite_note-1)\n* 19 January – Iran and [South Korea](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korea \"South Korea\") summon each other's [ambassadors](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambassador \"Ambassador\") in a deepening dispute between the countries, after [South Korean President](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korean_President \"South Korean President\") [Yoon Suk-yeol](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoon_Suk-yeol \"Yoon Suk-yeol\") called Iran \"the enemy of the [United Arab Emirates](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Arab_Emirates \"United Arab Emirates\")\" while addressing [South Korean troops](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_Korea_Army \"Republic of Korea Army\") stationed there.[[2]](#cite_note-2)\n* 24 January – Two [police officers](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_enforcement_in_Iran \"Law enforcement in Iran\") are killed and a third is injured in an attack in [Sistan and Baluchestan province](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sistan_and_Baluchestan_province \"Sistan and Baluchestan province\").[[3]](#cite_note-3)\n* 27 January – [Attack on the Azerbaijani Embassy in Tehran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attack_on_the_Azerbaijani_Embassy_in_Tehran \"Attack on the Azerbaijani Embassy in Tehran\"): A guard is killed and two others are injured during a shooting at the [Azerbaijani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azerbaijan \"Azerbaijan\") [embassy](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy \"Embassy\") in [Tehran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tehran \"Tehran\"). The perpetrator is arrested.[[4]](#cite_note-4)\n* 28 January – [Drone attacks](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Iran_drone_attacks \"2023 Iran drone attacks\") were reported across Iran.[[5]](#cite_note-5)\n\n* 23 February – Iran publicly acknowledges the [International Atomic Energy Agency](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Atomic_Energy_Agency \"International Atomic Energy Agency\") accusation it has [enriched uranium](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enriched_uranium \"Enriched uranium\") to 84%, bringing it close to developing a [nuclear weapon](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_weapon \"Nuclear weapon\"). The [Iranian government](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Iran \"Government of Iran\") maintains its nuclear program is \"completely peaceful\".[[6]](#cite_note-6)\n\n* 3 April – Two people are killed after heavy rain causes flash flooding across Iran.[[7]](#cite_note-7)\n* 8 April – [Police](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_Enforcement_Command_of_the_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran \"Law Enforcement Command of the Islamic Republic of Iran\") in Iran announce the installment of cameras in public places to identify and penalize women who do not observe [dressing codes](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dressing_code \"Dressing code\") for [hijabs](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hijab \"Hijab\"), while also urging citizens to confront women who are not sufficiently covered.[[8]](#cite_note-8)\n* 20 April – An [Iranian Navy](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_Navy \"Iranian Navy\") commander claims on state television that the Iranian Navy forced a U.S. submarine to surface as it transited the [Strait of Hormuz](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait_of_Hormuz \"Strait of Hormuz\") and that the submarine violated Iranian territorial waters. The U.S. denies the Iranian claims.[[9]](#cite_note-9)\n* 24 April – Iranian workers in major industries continue their [strike](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strike_action \"Strike action\") for a third day.[[10]](#cite_note-10)\n* 26 April\n  + Iranian [ayatollah](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayatollah \"Ayatollah\") and [Assembly of Experts](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assembly_of_Experts \"Assembly of Experts\") member [Abbas-Ali Soleimani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbas-Ali_Soleimani \"Abbas-Ali Soleimani\") is [assassinated](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination \"Assassination\") in a shooting at a bank in [Babolsar](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babolsar \"Babolsar\"), [Mazandaran province](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazandaran_province \"Mazandaran province\"). The perpetrator, a security guard at the bank, has been arrested by police.[[11]](#cite_note-11)\n  + Six Iranian demonstrators are injured in clashes in [Fanuj](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fanuj \"Fanuj\"), [Sistan and Baluchistan province](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sistan_and_Baluchistan_province \"Sistan and Baluchistan province\"), after a teenager was killed when his motorcycle collided with a police car.[[12]](#cite_note-12)\n* 30 April – [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") evacuates 65 nationals from [Sudan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudan \"Sudan\") with [Saudi Arabian](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudi_Arabia \"Saudi Arabia\") assistance.[[13]](#cite_note-13)\n\n* 19 May – Three men are [executed](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executed \"Executed\") in Iran. The three men were accused of \"moharebeh\" (\"waging war against God\"), killing three security officials in [Isfahan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isfahan \"Isfahan\") in November, and for alleged cooperation with the [MEK](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Mojahedin_Organization_of_Iran \"People's Mojahedin Organization of Iran\"). According to [human rights organizations](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_rights_organization \"Human rights organization\"), the men were denied due process, and were tortured and forced into televised confessions.[[14]](#cite_note-14)\n* 22 May – Five [Iranian border guards](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Border_Guard_Command_(Iran) \"Border Guard Command (Iran)\") are killed and two others are injured in [Saravan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saravan,_Iran \"Saravan, Iran\"), [Sistan and Baluchestan province](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sistan_and_Baluchestan_province \"Sistan and Baluchestan province\"), during a confrontation with an [armed group](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violent_non-state_actor \"Violent non-state actor\") at [the border](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran–Pakistan_border \"Iran–Pakistan border\") with [Pakistan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan \"Pakistan\").[[15]](#cite_note-15)\n\n* 1 June – A terrorist attack at the [Iran–Pakistan border](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran–Pakistan_border \"Iran–Pakistan border\") kills two Pakistani border patrol officers.[[16]](#cite_note-16)\n* 18 June – Fourteen people die from drinking [bootleg alcohol](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonshine \"Moonshine\") in [Alborz province](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alborz_province \"Alborz province\").[[17]](#cite_note-17)\n\n* 15 July – State media reports morality police will resume headscarf patrols.[[18]](#cite_note-18)\n\n* 3 September – [Foreign Minister](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_Foreign_Affairs_(Iran) \"Minister of Foreign Affairs (Iran)\") [Hossein Amir-Abdollahian](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Amir-Abdollahian \"Hossein Amir-Abdollahian\") says that [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") has started talks to revive the [Joint Comprehensive Plan of Action](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joint_Comprehensive_Plan_of_Action \"Joint Comprehensive Plan of Action\").[[19]](#cite_note-19)\n* 16 September – [Human rights](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_rights_in_Iran \"Human rights in Iran\") organizations say that [Iranian police](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_police \"Iranian police\") arrested the father of [Mahsa Amini](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahsa_Amini \"Mahsa Amini\") on the first anniversary of [her death](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Mahsa_Amini \"Death of Mahsa Amini\").[[20]](#cite_note-20)\n* 18 September – Iran announced that [a prisoner swap](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_2023_Iran–United_States_prisoner_release \"September 2023 Iran–United States prisoner release\") will take place today with the United States. Under the agreement, Iran will also have access to 6 billion [dollars](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_dollar \"United States dollar\") frozen in [South Korea](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korea \"South Korea\").[[21]](#cite_note-21)\n\n* 3 November – [Langarud drug rehabilitation center fire](/\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 10000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
